<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>BBC News</title><subtitle type="html">BBC News - Technology</subtitle><id>https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:21:58Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss.xml" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/technology" /><link rel="via" href="https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Can the Zelda remake capture the magic of the original?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm8xznl0n1q4o#0</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:21:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T00:37:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm8xznl0n1q4o--e3d6f99e0ff0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm8xznl0n1q4o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Nintendo has released its remake of what is considered one of the best games ever made - the BBC's Tom Gerken gives his verdict.</summary></entry><entry><title>Elon Musk appears to signal the end of the road for Cybertruck</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq1j33w7d232o#0</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T21:49:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq1j33w7d232o--25cd541ca220.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq1j33w7d232o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Musk said it was to make room for production of its Cybercabs - autonomous taxis without a driver.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI stocks climb after trillions wiped from market values</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c35ynnpzdq51o#0</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T21:06:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c35ynnpzdq51o--de0c28c9953f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c35ynnpzdq51o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Investors had been selling off tech shares in part due to concerns the Democrat election victory would mean slower AI development.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why the US midterms sparked an AI stock selloff</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crlykkzwwpydo#0</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T18:32:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crlykkzwwpydo--01856f52ceb4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crlykkzwwpydo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Fears of more AI regulation appear to have sparked fear among investors, but  concerns about the industry have been growing for some time.</summary></entry><entry><title>Global stocks plunge as fears over US AI slowdown spread to Asia and Europe</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmn04705rd8jo#0</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:25:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmn04705rd8jo--7f806f4d6ebc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmn04705rd8jo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Investors have reacted to possible tougher scrutiny of data centre construction and the AI industry.</summary></entry><entry><title>The engine parts that 'fight the laws of the universe'</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwe9lmp1pyyxo#0</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T00:06:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwe9lmp1pyyxo--3880731809db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwe9lmp1pyyxo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Investment has surged into the making of jet turbine blades - an extremely difficult component to make.</summary></entry><entry><title>Elon Musk's millions failed to deliver Republican wins in fierce midterms</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cv8ez3p3ge5ko#0</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:41:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cv8ez3p3ge5ko--5420898fdc12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cv8ez3p3ge5ko?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Musk spent nearly $500m in the 2026 US midterm elections, an individual election spending record.</summary></entry><entry><title>French blood storage impacted by freezer hacks as theories swirl about culprits</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c8vgxyvz6y9ro#0</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:26:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c8vgxyvz6y9ro--91fc8537a51a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c8vgxyvz6y9ro?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The French Blood Establishment (EFS) said cold rooms storing blood were impacted by hackers.</summary></entry><entry><title>Graduates are managing AI - but are they learning much else?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c820vz6wyp65o#0</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T00:04:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c820vz6wyp65o--4f07d3c53b71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c820vz6wyp65o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Graduates are spending more time managing AI, but are they missing out on other work experience?</summary></entry><entry><title>Binance says fake job interviews used as part of $6.3bn crypto hack</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck5ynwz9gy67o#0</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:19:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck5ynwz9gy67o--6b6c7100781c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck5ynwz9gy67o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">An engineer was contacted through a legitimate job-hunting platform and invited to bogus job interviews with fake company representatives, Binance says.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK meat industry hit by cyber-attack which targeted European supermarket freezers</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckq6ndq8l6v0o#0</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckq6ndq8l6v0o--a4648347bec4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckq6ndq8l6v0o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Supermarkets in countries including Ireland, Sweden  and Belgium reported fridges being hiked in temperature on Monday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Apple unsure when it will get more foldable iPhones ahead of Christmas</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6n8dn457ypko#0</id><updated>2026-11-08T06:20:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:10:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6n8dn457ypko--9da12d45db34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6n8dn457ypko?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The tech giant reports strong sales but admits "constraints" are affecting supplies of the iPhone Duo.</summary></entry><entry><title>North Korea denies being behind record $6.3bn Binance hack</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/arti